#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166494 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccfebb3-3017-5639-8b67-058c304c9df8" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Binomial CDF Table"}] :question/id #uuid "56d68682-0e4d-57e5-9441-997cf4d33f29" :question/math-academy-id "e-15052" :question/problem "Consider the binomial random variable $X\\sim B(7, 0.63)$. Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing values in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X \\leq x)$ | $0.0009$ | $0.0123$ | $0.0701$ | $0.2341$ | $0.5134$ | $0.7987$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\displaystyle \\binom{n}{x} p^x (1-p)^{n-x}, \\qquad x=0,1,2,\\ldots,n\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=7$ and $p=0.63$.\n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n- For $F(6)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(6) &= P(X \\le 6) \\\\\n&= P(X \\le 5) + P(X = 6) \\\\\n&= F(5) + P(X = 6) \\\\\n&= 0.7987 + (\\frac{7}{6})(0.63)^{6}(1 - 0.63)^{7 - 6} \\\\\n&= 0.7987 + 7 \\cdot (0.63)^{6} \\cdot (0.37)^{1} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.9606\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Since $n=7$, we have that $F(7) = P(X\\leq 7) = 1$.\n\nTherefore, our completed table looks as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X \\leq x)$ | $0.0009$ | $0.0123$ | $0.0701$ | $0.2341$ | $0.5134$ | $0.7987$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.9606}$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166495 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69c62fd8-05af-57dc-a96c-4dcba884ea32" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Using the CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "92a73e93-f882-5329-a19c-00a6a270bced" :question/math-academy-id "e-15054" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.67)$ given below, compute $P(X=2)$.\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0013\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0969\\,$ | $\\,0.3130\\,$ | $\\,0.6422\\,$ | $\\,0.9095\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(2) &= P(X \\le 2) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {0, 1, 2}) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {0, 1}) + P(X = 2) \\\\\n&= P(X \\le 1) + P(X = 2) \\\\\n&= F(1) + P(X = 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X = 2) &= F(2) - F(1) \\\\\n&= 0.0969 - 0.0170 \\\\\n&= 0.0799\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166496 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f0c914d-f2c0-5641-9818-312eac10d1b4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Over an Interval Using the CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "c80fb077-2d31-522b-8083-5a72613f84de" :question/math-academy-id "e-15055" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.47)$ given below, compute $P(1 \\leq X \\lt 5)$.\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0222\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.4015\\,$ | $\\,0.7107\\,$ | $\\,0.9163\\,$ | $\\,0.9892\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(4) &= P(X \\le 4) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {0, 1, 2, 3, 4}) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {0}) + P(X ∈ {1, 2, 3, 4}) \\\\\n&= P(X \\le 0) + P(1 \\le X < 5) \\\\\n&= F(0) + P(1 \\le X < 5)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(1 \\le X < 5) &= F(4) - F(0) \\\\\n&= 0.9163 - 0.0222 \\\\\n&= 0.8941\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166497 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95b5e3bd-0e7e-56df-80d5-be39de76da16" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Binomial Probability Over an Interval Containing a \"Greater Than\" Symbol"}] :question/id #uuid "c9a6a708-925d-54aa-ac0a-023e5259d19a" :question/math-academy-id "e-15056" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(7, 0.52)$ given below, compute $P(X \\geq 2)$.\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0059\\,$ | $\\,0.0504\\,$ | $\\,0.1951\\,$ | $\\,0.4563\\,$ | $\\,0.7393\\,$ | $\\,0.9233\\,$ | $\\,0.9897\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a)\n$$\n\nNow, note that\n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 2) = P(X \\gt 1)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X \\ge 2) &= P(X > 1) \\\\\n&= 1 - P(X \\le 1) \\\\\n&= 1 - F(1) \\\\\n&= 1 - 0.0504 \\\\\n&= 0.9496\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccfebb3-3017-5639-8b67-058c304c9df8" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Binomial CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "b69d6c50-4593-518f-9ffd-5e85fb9bb8a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163919} {:answer-field/id #uuid "7f7f40b0-78f3-55c9-9c52-0b2466a01973" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163920}] :question/id #uuid "2747e086-f93d-5020-86de-46c90085c6ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-224463" :question/problem "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6, 0.26)$. Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing values in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X \\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $0.8144$ | $0.9569$ | $0.9944$ | $0.9997$ | $1.0000$ |"}]}
